window.DM_BENCHX={"meta":{"last":"2026-11-10","n_all":1256,"built":"2026-11-11","note":"Outside figures are quoted from their publishers and kept apart from Dream Menu data. They measure different things (polls of all adults, delivery orders, menus, sales), so a difference is a finding, not an error."},"items":[{"id":"pineapple","topic":"Pineapple on pizza","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"level","dm":{"v":49.3,"unit":"%","text":"49.3% say yes","base":"1,230 guests"},"ext":{"v":53,"unit":"%","text":"53% of Britons like pineapple on pizza","who":"YouGov, GB adults","date":"2017","url":"https://yougov.co.uk/news/2017/03/06/does-pineapple-belong-pizza"},"read":"Foodies split almost exactly like the general public. Pineapple is a genuine 50:50 call, so it belongs on a pizza menu as an option, not a statement."},{"id":"tea","topic":"Tea or coffee","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"level","dm":{"v":67.4,"unit":"%","text":"67.4% pick coffee (25.4% tea)","base":"957 guests"},"ext":{"v":35,"unit":"%","text":"Just over a third of Britons prefer coffee; 52% prefer tea","who":"YouGov, GB adults","date":"2012","url":"https://yougov.co.uk/news/2012/03/27/tea-vs-coffee"},"read":"Dream Menu guests are far more coffee-led than Britain as a whole. That reflects who answers (younger, urban, many in the trade), so read coffee demand here as the leading edge, not the national average. YouGov Profiles data from 2025 shows daily coffee and tea drinking now close to level across age groups."},{"id":"irnbru","topic":"Irn-Bru or Coke","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"level","dm":{"v":46.1,"unit":"%","text":"46.1% pick Irn-Bru (33.4% Coke)","base":"1,229 guests"},"ext":{"v":21,"unit":"%","text":"Irn-Bru was 21% of 330ml cans sold with Scottish takeaways, against 36% for Coke","who":"Scoffable takeaway orders, Scotland","date":"2022","url":"https://www.scoffable.com/article/irnbru-vs-coke-ten-years-of-takeaway-data"},"extra":"AG Barr says Irn-Bru accounts for one in every two flavoured fizzy drink cans in Scotland and grew ahead of the soft-drinks market (Circana, 12 weeks to 18 July 2026).","read":"Irn-Bru wins the loyalty question; Coke wins the order that comes with a takeaway meal. Both are true: one is identity, the other is habit. A range in Scotland needs both, with Irn-Bru as the local signal."},{"id":"water","topic":"Tap water with dinner","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"level","dm":{"v":34.7,"unit":"%","text":"34.7% ask for tap water","base":"1,230 guests"},"ext":{"v":33,"unit":"%","text":"About a third of people drink tap water when eating out in restaurants","who":"Local Government Association survey, 3,000 people","date":"2016","url":"https://www.yorkshirepost.co.uk/health/tap-water-should-be-offered-families-eating-out-1799806"},"read":"Roughly one diner in three takes tap water in both sources. The rest split between still and sparkling, so a bottled water offer still matters to two tables in three."},{"id":"matcha","topic":"Matcha","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"The trend guests most want binned: 115 guests (9% of all interviews)","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Consumers choosing matcha lattes 33.5% more than a year earlier; matcha dishes on UK menus doubled","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer and menu data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"extra":"A matcha iced latte was one of the UK’s top trending Deliveroo orders of 2025.","read":"Growth and backlash at once: the classic sign of a polarising trend near its peak. Serve it well for the fans who want it, but don’t build a menu identity around it."},{"id":"pistachio","topic":"Dubai chocolate and pistachio","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Second most-named trend to bin: 105 guests (8% of interviews)","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Pistachio reaching consumers 44% faster than a year earlier; pistachio with chocolate up 28%","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"The same pattern as matcha. Pistachio as a flavour still has room; the viral Dubai bar format is what foodies are tired of."},{"id":"loaded","topic":"Loaded and dirty food","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"38 guests name loaded and dirty food as a trend to bin","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Loaded fries and shareable potato platters recommended as plant-forward wins for pubs and bars","who":"UKHospitality trend report","date":"2026","url":"https://www.ukhospitality.org.uk/?p=10357"},"read":"A gap between what the trade is advised to add and what foodies say they are tired of. Worth testing before adding loaded formats to a menu."},{"id":"tiramisu","topic":"Tiramisu","theme":"Dishes","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"flat","text":"Steady staple: 12.2% of dessert answers, between 10.3% and 14.5% in every full quarter","base":"dessert answers"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Tiramisu up nearly 15% in consumer demand","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"The biggest single dessert on the Dream Menu, and still growing in the wider market. As safe as dessert gets."},{"id":"ooh","topic":"How often Scotland eats out","theme":"Market","tier":"public","verdict":"context","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"Dream Menu asks what people would choose, not how often they buy","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"text":"Out-of-home transactions in Scotland fell 7% in 2025, to 809 million; delivery transactions fell 30%","who":"Food Standards Scotland, Worldpanel by Numerator","date":"2026","url":"https://www.foodstandards.gov.scot/science-and-evidence/monitoring-out-of-home-food-and-drink-purchases-in-scotland-and-great-britain-2024-2025"},"read":"Fewer trips make each visit count for more. Dream Menu shows what people want from the visits they still make: the dishes worth leaving the house for."},{"id":"sites","topic":"Venues trading","theme":"Market","tier":"public","verdict":"context","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"Guests have named 1,935 venues","base":"venue mentions"},"ext":{"text":"Britain had 98,319 licensed venues in September 2026, 977 fewer than a year earlier (−1.0%)","who":"NIQ Hospitality Market Monitor (CGA data)","date":"October 2026","url":"https://www.vinetur.com/en/20261030110108/britain-lost-977-licensed-hospitality-venues-in-the-year-to-september.html"},"read":"A shrinking market concentrates demand. The venues guests name repeatedly are the ones with a reason to visit that survives a squeeze."},{"id":"roast","topic":"Sunday roast","theme":"Dishes","tier":"partner","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Share of main answers: 5.2% earlier, 2.6% recent (−2.6 pts, a clear move)","base":"main answers"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Consumer demand for Sunday roast up 11.6% in a year","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"People still eat roasts, but fewer name one as their dream main. A habit, not an aspiration: keep it on for Sunday trade, and don’t expect it to drive a new opening."},{"id":"sides","topic":"Sides: fries against greens","theme":"Dishes","tier":"partner","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Potatoes and fries 45.1% → 33.7% of side answers; vegetables and salad 14.1% → 19.7% (both clear moves)","base":"side answers"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Operators growing the number and price of sides to lift spend; vegetable dishes present but not leading menu growth","who":"Lumina Intelligence Menu Tracker, 80 UK chains","date":"2025 to May 2026","url":"https://www.lumina-intelligence.com/?p=41434"},"read":"Menus are adding sides; guests are switching which sides they want. The opportunity for a supplier is greens, seasonal veg and salads priced as an upsell, not more fries."},{"id":"cocktails","topic":"Cocktails","theme":"Drinks","tier":"partner","verdict":"agrees","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Share of alcoholic drink answers: 72.1% earlier, 53.8% recent (−18.2 pts, a clear move)","base":"drink answers, original question"},"ext":{"dir":"down","text":"Espresso martini down 15%, Aperol spritz down 14%, mojito down 13% in consumer demand","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"Both sources show cocktails cooling. Guests are moving to whisky, lager and beer."},{"id":"whisky","topic":"Whisky","theme":"Drinks","tier":"partner","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"up","text":"Share of alcoholic drink answers: 3.1% earlier, 9.6% recent (+6.6 pts, a clear move)","base":"drink answers, original question"},"ext":{"dir":"down","text":"Diageo’s Great Britain spirits sales fell by a mid-single-digit percentage in early 2026","who":"Diageo trading update via Morning Advertiser","date":"May 2026","url":"https://www.morningadvertiser.co.uk/Article/2026/05/06/demand-for-guinness-contributes-to-diageo-sales-growth/"},"extra":"Scotland is different: whisky’s on-trade sales value in Scotland grew 18.2% in 2023, giving Scotland 15.4% of UK on-trade whisky sales (CGA by NIQ).","read":"A Scottish story running against the national spirits market. Whisky is rising on Dream Menu because the panel is mostly Scottish, where whisky has been gaining on-trade share. Treat it as a Scotland range priority, not a UK one."},{"id":"guinness","topic":"Guinness","theme":"Drinks","tier":"partner","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"flat","text":"Guinness and stout, share of alcoholic drink answers: 4.8% earlier, 2.7% recent (−2.1 pts, within noise)","base":"drink answers, original question"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"One in nine pints poured in the UK is a Guinness; the UK’s number-one on-trade beer with double-digit growth","who":"CGA by NIQ via Marketing Week; Diageo","date":"2025 to 2026","url":"https://www.marketingweek.com/guinness-women-younger-drinkers/"},"read":"The market’s biggest beer story barely registers as a dream drink. Guinness is what people order, not what they dream of; beer as a whole is rising on Dream Menu, led by lager."},{"id":"cake","topic":"Cheesecake and big cakes","theme":"Dishes","tier":"partner","verdict":"agrees","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Baked cheesecake, share of dessert answers: 7.9% earlier, 4.0% recent (−3.9 pts, a clear move)","base":"dessert answers"},"ext":{"dir":"down","text":"Chocolate cake down 24%, cupcakes down 38%, birthday cake down 41% in consumer demand","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"Cake fatigue shows in both. The desserts holding up are tiramisu, sticky toffee pudding and lighter, fruit-led plates."},{"id":"confidence","topic":"Operator confidence","theme":"Market","tier":"partner","verdict":"context","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"Look Ahead operators rate the next 12 months 6.2 out of 10","base":"55 operators, mostly micro and small"},"ext":{"text":"51% of hospitality leaders confident about the next 12 months; only 16% of independents","who":"NIQ and Zonal Business Confidence Survey, leaders of 16,000+ sites","date":"Feb to Mar 2026","url":"https://www.morningadvertiser.co.uk/Article/2026/04/01/hospitality-confidence-rebounds-but-costs-hit-small-pubs-and-operators"},"read":"Dream Menu’s operators are small independents, the group NIQ finds least confident. Their middling score is in line with that: cautious, not collapsing."},{"id":"prices","topic":"Prices","theme":"Market","tier":"partner","verdict":"agrees","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"89% of operators see supplier prices rising","base":"53 operators"},"ext":{"text":"Restaurant and hotel prices up 3.8% in the year to September 2026, against 3.5% for all prices","who":"Office for National Statistics, CPI","date":"October 2026","url":"https://www.babypips.com/news/headline-uk-inflation-september-2026-cpi-fuel-prices-boe-rate-hike"},"read":"Costs are still rising faster than prices overall, which is why operators are reaching for supplier renegotiation and menu engineering first."}]};
